<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kohima</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kohima was fought from April to June 1944 at Kohima in the Naga Hills of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, as part of the Japanese offensive against India. The small British and Indian garrison held out, fighting at close quarters across the deputy commissioner's tennis court, until relieved, and the Japanese 31st Division was forced to retreat. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-imphal">Battle of Imphal</a> it marked the turning point of the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kohima.jpg" alt="Battle of Kohima" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Official photographer of No.9 Army Film and Photographic Unit. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IND_003698_Garrison_Hill_Kohima.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
